# FIX-PERSONA-01 green - same test, same command, after pinning the harness project

Date 2026-10-28. Host macOS arm64. JDK: Homebrew openjdk 21.0.12.1 via JAVA_HOME only; no system
Java was installed and no system configuration was changed. Maven 3.10.0.
Baseline SHA (red): dc7d0723daacca43c321b7d3a32d6b99c78f09c6  = main a409140 + the new test only
Fix SHA (green):    ff8666de1d1960b47fb70bd014ecbfd79efecfdd
Test: services/agent-runtime/src/test/java/com/workpal/runtime/RuntimeProjectIsolationTest.java
      -> startupDirectoryAgentsMdNeverReachesTheModel
Command (identical for red and green):
  export JAVA_HOME=<jdk21>; export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
  mvn -B -f services/agent-runtime/pom.xml test -Dtest=RuntimeProjectIsolationTest
No real model, no scripted runtime and no capture proxy: the test drives RuntimeEngine.execute
against a recording fixture model on 127.0.0.1 and asserts on the captured request body.
Host paths below are replaced with <worktree>. No credential appears in these files.

Note on the assertions: the canary, launch-path and persona assertions are unchanged between red
and green, and the canary one is what failed at baseline. A third assertion that demanded the
agents_context tag be ABSENT was over-specified for a rejected fix (disableWorkspaceContext) and
now requires the block to carry no CONTENT, which is the actual property; pinning the project
leaves an empty <agents_context/>. Recorded here rather than left implicit.

